<resources xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools">
    <!-- Launch theme only. The real design language is Compose-side in
         ui/theme/ (Instrument, decided 2026-08-01, wayfinder ticket 02).

         This exists so the window background matches the Compose ground before
         the first frame draws. It was Theme.Material.Light.NoActionBar, which
         flashed white on every cold start against a near-black app.

         The ground and bar tone come from launch_ground / launch_light_bars, which values-notnight
         sets to Typeset paper with dark icons (home-ui review 2026-11-18): by day the app opens on
         paper, so a black first frame flashed. The phone's own theme is all a resource can know;
         bedtime, the one-tap switch and Matrix mode are applied by Compose on the first frame. -->
    <style name="Theme.Legion" parent="android:Theme.Material.NoActionBar">
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@color/launch_ground</item>
        <item name="android:statusBarColor">@color/launch_ground</item>
        <item name="android:navigationBarColor">@color/launch_ground</item>
        <item name="android:windowLightStatusBar" tools:targetApi="m">@bool/launch_light_bars</item>
    </style>
</resources>
